            <ArticleTitle>Chronic pain: a difficult problem.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>433-47</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The author discusses the general problem of the small but significant population of people in whom pain persists for months or years after a precipitating event, such as a hand injury. The nature of pain, the perception of pain, and characteristics of chronic pain patients are discussed, as well as evaluation and treatment of chronic pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
